{"repositoryId":1314148301,"availability":"available","full":"yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet","name":"claude-code-cheatsheet","description":"A workflow-first cheat sheet for Claude Code - nine steps from empty prompt to merged PR, plus every command, flag, key, model, and the memory/hooks/skills/agents that make it yours.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-27T18:16:38Z","updated":"2026-07-27T18:16:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yoavstern-1.github.io/claude-code-cheatsheet/","topics":["anthropic","cheatsheet","claude","claude-code","developer-tools","pwa"],"demo":"https://yoavstern-1.github.io/claude-code-cheatsheet/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.833Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.833Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.833Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.833Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A workflow-first reference for Claude Code: nine steps from an empty prompt to a merged pull request, plus every command, flag, key and model behind them — and the memory files, hooks, skills and subagents that make it yours.","Most cheat sheets are a wall of commands sorted alphabetically. That tells you what exists, but not what to do with it.","Knowing that /compact exists was never the hard part. The hard part is knowing when to reach for it, which model to open the session on, and why the session that was sharp an hour ago is now slow and stupid. So the reference here hangs off a workflow instead of an index."],"features":["Ctrl+K, or just /. Fuzzy subsequence matching with a bonus for consecutive hits, so you type what you half-remember and it fills in the rest. cmpct finds /compact; wrktr finds --worktree.","It searches commands, workflow steps, patterns and guides together. ↵ copies a command or jumps to the section. Ctrl+↵ pins it.","Every launch flag, slash command, keybinding and config file path, grouped by what you're trying to do rather than by first letter. Click a card to copy it. Star it and it lands in Pinned.","Five mechanisms decide how Claude behaves before you type a word — memory, slash commands, skills, hooks and subagents. The tab routes you to the right one by the sentence you keep repeating, then shows the file that…","Running everything on the biggest model is the most common and most expensive mistake. A grep does not need Opus."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9e63256b27b67216847d2ddbe2804075cc5d9c52dfe82d1f1732d1ab35f7b75d","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.940Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.940Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A workflow-first reference for Claude Code: nine steps from an empty prompt to a merged pull request, plus every command, flag, key and model behind them — and the memory files, hooks, skills and subagents that make it yours.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"It runs on Chrome's built-in on-device model, so there's no API key, no account, and nothing leaves your machine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9e63256b27b67216847d2ddbe2804075cc5d9c52dfe82d1f1732d1ab35f7b75d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.941Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-27T18:16:44Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yoavstern-1/claude-code-cheatsheet/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:08.942Z","hash":"9e63256b27b67216847d2ddbe2804075cc5d9c52dfe82d1f1732d1ab35f7b75d","originalBytes":9896,"storedBytes":9896,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["command","claude","